  <h2 id="tools">Tools</h2>

  <h3 id="functions">The function-calling loop</h3>
  <p>
    The single most important code shape in the exam. The model <em>decides</em>; your code <em>executes</em>; you feed
    the result back keyed by <code>call_id</code>. Missing the loop, or missing the <code>call_id</code>, are the two
    classic broken snippets.
  </p>

  <CodeBlock code={functionLoop} lang="python" label="Python · function calling" />

  <Callout type="warn" title="Three failure modes in that loop">
    <ul style="margin-bottom:0">
      <li><strong>No loop.</strong> Handling only the first round means chained or parallel tool calls are dropped and the model never produces a final answer.</li>
      <li><strong>Missing <code>call_id</code>.</strong> The service cannot match the output to the call, and the model sees an unanswered tool call.</li>
      <li><strong>Tools omitted on the follow-up call.</strong> Pass <code>tools=</code> again so the model can still call them on the next round.</li>
    </ul>
  </Callout>

  <h3 id="built-in">Built-in tools</h3>
  <CodeBlock code={builtInTools} lang="python" label="Python · built-in tools" />

