  <h2 id="agents">Agent lifecycle</h2>
  <CodeBlock code={agentLifecycle} lang="python" label="Python · agents" />

  <Callout type="code-note" title="Reading agent code correctly">
    <ul style="margin-bottom:0">
      <li><code>create_version</code> is both create <em>and</em> update: every call snapshots a new <strong>immutable version</strong>, which is what makes rollback and comparison possible.</li>
      <li>The agent is addressed by <strong>name</strong>, not id, when binding a client to it.</li>
      <li>A <strong>prompt agent</strong> is a <code>PromptAgentDefinition</code>. A <strong>hosted agent</strong> ships your container or .zip instead and calls the project endpoint from inside.</li>
      <li>Calling the Responses API directly with inline <code>instructions</code> and <code>tools</code> and no agent resource is an <strong>ephemeral agent</strong>.</li>
    </ul>
  </Callout>

