  <h2 id="evaluation">Evaluation</h2>
  <CodeBlock code={evaluation} lang="python" label="Python · evaluation" />

  <p>
    The <code>data</code> file is JSON Lines with the columns each evaluator needs — typically
    <code>query</code>, <code>context</code>, <code>response</code> and sometimes <code>ground_truth</code>.
    AI-assisted evaluators need a <strong>judge model</strong> configured. Passing
    <code>azure_ai_project</code> publishes the run to the portal so results are visible alongside traces.
  </p>

  <!-- ================================================================= -->
  <h2 id="tracing">Tracing</h2>
  <CodeBlock code={tracing} lang="python" label="Python · tracing" />

  <Callout type="warn" title="Content recording is off by default — deliberately">
    <p>
      Traces capture the call tree without prompt and completion text unless you opt in. That default exists because
      prompts routinely contain customer data. If a question asks why traces show spans but no prompt text, the answer
      is the content-recording setting — and the follow-up consideration is whether your retention policy permits it.
    </p>
  </Callout>

  <!-- ================================================================= -->
  <h2 id="search-sdk">Azure AI Search from Python</h2>
  <CodeBlock code={search} lang="python" label="Python · search" />

  <Callout type="exam" title="What to look for in a search snippet">
    <ul style="margin-bottom:0">
      <li><code>search_text</code> alone = keyword only. <code>vector_queries</code> alone = vector only. <strong>Both = hybrid</strong>, merged with RRF.</li>
      <li><code>query_type="semantic"</code> plus a <code>semantic_configuration_name</code> = semantic reranking. Without the configuration it fails.</li>
      <li><code>VectorizableTextQuery</code> means the index has a <strong>vectorizer</strong> and embeds the query for you; <code>VectorizedQuery</code> means you supplied the vector yourself.</li>
      <li><code>filter</code> applies to <strong>text fields only</strong>.</li>
      <li>Keyless search needs a <strong>data-plane role</strong> on the search service, not just a control-plane one.</li>
    </ul>
  </Callout>

  <!-- ================================================================= -->
  <h2 id="migration">Classic to new: the migration map</h2>
  <p>
    Older samples, blog posts and practice questions use the classic shapes. Recognise them and know the replacement.
  </p>

  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="tbl t-green">
      <thead><tr><th>Classic (Agents v1 / Assistants)</th><th>Current (Agents v2 / Responses)</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>AzureOpenAI(api_key=..., api_version="2024-xx-xx")</code></td><td><code>AIProjectClient(endpoint, credential).get_openai_client()</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>client.beta.assistants.create(...)</code></td><td><code>project.agents.create_version(agent_name, definition=PromptAgentDefinition(...))</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>client.beta.threads.create()</code></td><td><code>openai.conversations.create()</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>threads.messages.create(...)</code></td><td>Conversation <strong>items</strong>, or just <code>input=</code> on the response</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>threads.runs.create_and_poll(...)</code></td><td><code>openai.responses.create(conversation=...)</code> — no polling loop</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>chat.completions.create(messages=[...])</code></td><td><code>responses.create(input=[...])</code> (chat completions still exists for plain model calls)</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>run.required_action.submit_tool_outputs</code></td><td><code>function_call_output</code> items with a <code>call_id</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Monthly <code>api-version</code> query parameters</td><td>Stable <code>/openai/v1/</code> routes</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>azure-ai-inference</code>, <code>azure-ai-generative</code>, <code>azure-ai-ml</code></td><td><code>azure-ai-projects</code> 2.x</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <Callout type="tip" title="A three-second triage for any snippet">
    <p>
      See <code>threads</code>, <code>runs</code>, <code>assistants</code>, <code>submit_tool_outputs</code> or an
      <code>api_version</code> string? It is <strong>classic</strong>. See <code>AIProjectClient</code>,
      <code>responses</code>, <code>conversations</code> or <code>create_version</code>? It is
      <strong>current</strong>. If a question asks you to modernise code, that mapping is the whole answer.
    </p>
  </Callout>

